    "title": "The same section has two schedules",
    "reading": ["The basins, stepped edges and exposed water channels give the square a legible relationship between collection, movement and temporary storage. The critical architectural reading is the change of state: a surface available for recreation is also reserved for water. The section has to make sense in both conditions.", "De Urbanisten distinguishes shallower basins receiving local runoff from a deeper basin serving a larger catchment during sustained rainfall. That design explanation helps connect the square to its surroundings. It does not establish how much water was stored during this visit or how quickly the space returned to use."],
    "takeaway": "The square's development value can be investigated beyond the area of its basins: it reserves space for a service that may benefit surrounding streets and properties. But shared use creates an operational obligation too. Cleaning, drainage and the return to recreation belong in the evaluation alongside designed storage capacity.",
