    "title": "The control room as a research viewpoint",
    "reading": ["The guided visit and control-room photograph provide a different entry into water infrastructure from a view of the lock as an urban landmark. They locate the research at the place where an operating system is supervised. The photograph documents access to that setting; it should not be made to stand in for an operator's account of a particular event.", "The analytical question is how water levels and different forms of movement are coordinated over time. Compared with Maeslantkering's exceptional protective action, Parksluizen directs attention toward recurring transitions. A useful next record would follow one complete cycle and identify the decisions and dependencies at each stage."],
